Linux cross-RBE fix: export build_tar for the main repo's host-constrained helper.

MongoDB's install archives preserve source mtimes and therefore run locally on
the client host. During PPC64LE and s390x cross-RBE builds, rules_pkg otherwise
builds build_tar's Python launcher for the x86_64 execution platform and then
tries to execute it on the native IBM host.

rules_pkg exports build_tar.py so the main repository can define a
host-constrained build_tar_host helper (see //bazel/rules_pkg/BUILD) from the
local host constraints of its own generated platform repository. Bazel 9
bzlmod cannot resolve @local_config_platform from inside a module repository —
the legacy built-in is gone and root-module repos are invisible to module
repos — so the helper must live in the main repository. The internal py_libraries it
depends on are widened to public visibility so the main repo can depend on
them. Callers pass the helper via the new build_tar_tool attribute (see
pkg_tar_tool_override.patch).

Applied via `single_version_override(patches=...)` on rules_pkg in
//MODULE.bazel. Candidate for upstreaming to bazelbuild/rules_pkg.

--- a/pkg/private/tar/BUILD
+++ b/pkg/private/tar/BUILD
@@ -19,3 +19,8 @@
 load("@rules_python//python:defs.bzl", "py_binary", "py_library")
 
+exports_files(
+    ["build_tar.py"],
+    visibility = ["//visibility:public"],
+)
+
 package(
 
